the Tang is...?

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:36.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is a text chain that I hav
with Paula Pell, Tina Fey,

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:40.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ana Gasteyer, Rachel Dratch,
Maya Rudolph, and me.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who am I leaving out?
Amy Poehler.

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:44.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a pretty good group
of people.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's the funnest.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what I would --
the funnest.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know would what I
would do without it.

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:52.505 size:84% position:42%
I would not get through
this, like, turd hoagie

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:55.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is 2020 without the Tang.
-The funnest.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you are
being Brechtian again.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.744 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, so Brechtian.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was so withering
when he said that.

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:03.749 line:92%
I was like, "Can I kill myself?"

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:09.322
-I remember you and Amy
at the read-through table

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
were close enough
that you could pass notes.

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I was right next to Dratch.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:16.162 line:92%
Dratch and I were note sharers

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-It was a great gift

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:20.766
because those were the mos
stressful times of the week.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:21.934 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, my God, horrible.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:25.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were your note passing days
with Poehler wonderful?

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:27.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God, they were so w-
well, you know --

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:28.875 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like, constantly --

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:33.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, Seth, next time I'm on
or maybe at my funeral

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're speaking
at my funeral,

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.850
I'll read what you -- 'cause
we used to pass notes too.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:43.556
But my favorite note that
Poehler ever passed me was

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.625 line:92%
I think, you know, "Jostie" --

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
Colin Jost used to come in
looking like

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
